==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|corymbus}}

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|corymbe}}, from the {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|corymbus}}, from the {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|κόρυμβος}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{enPR|kŏʹrĭmb}}, {{IPA|/ˈkɒɹɪmb/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|botany}} A [[cluster#Noun|cluster]] of [[flower#Noun|flowers]] with a [[flat#Adjective|flat]] or [[convex]] top.
#* {{quote-journal|lang=en|author=T. Appleby|title=Plants for Baskets|editors=George W. Johnson and [[w:Robert Hogg (biologist)|Robert Hogg]]|journal=The Cottage Gardener, and Country Gentleman’s Companion: A Journal of Horticulture, Rural and Domestic Economy, Botany, and Natural History|location=London|publisher=Published for the proprietors,{{nb...|20, Paternoster-Row}}|date=5 June 1855|volume=XIV|issue=CCCXLIX|page=161|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=-EoCAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA161|column=2|oclc=503937615|passage=''Hoya carnosa'' (Thick-leaved).—Foliage large, flowers in large drooping '''corymbs'''; they are of a pinkish-white colour, and contain, or rather yield, drops of pure sweet honey; hence this fine old plant is known as the Honey plant.}}

